WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.320
Spoiler alert!

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.600
No one is safe.

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.960
When your favorite TV show wants to make an
impact, it's pretty much guaranteed that your

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.240
favorite character is going to die.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:14.700
Everyone is expendable when it comes to generating
buzz, and 2016 was an especially rough year

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.240
for TV deaths.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.720
After you're done watching our first video
about TV's most recent dearly deceased, prepare

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:26.740
yourself for some more spoilers with some
of the most upsetting TV deaths of 2016.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.460
Barb

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:33.010
In spite of being a collection of warm '80s
nostalgia, the award-winning Stranger Things

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.200
is decidedly at home in today's TV landscape.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.300
It's not afraid to kill off its characters,
and that includes innocent, nerdy children.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:45.210
The Netflix hit raised the stakes pretty high
when the show's resident Milhouse, lonely,

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:49.350
geeky Barb was suddenly taken by the flower-faced
beast from the Upside-Down.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:54.120
Sure, her death gave her best friend Nancy
and Will's brother Jonathan a reason to team

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:59.530
up and go monster hunting, but not soon enough
to save poor Barb… who was pretty much forgotten

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:01.000
for the rest of the season.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.140
Season Two promises to get justice for Barb,
however, according to the Duffer Brothers,

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:06.970
the show's creators.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:08.240
Poussey

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.000
An inmate at Litchfield since the start of
the Netflix dramedy, Poussey was a fan-favorite

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.600
with a particularly heartbreaking backstory.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.490
In season 4, Poussey started a relationship
with fellow inmate Soso, as well as a friendship

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:24.869
with jailed TV chef Judy King, who promised
her a job upon release.

00:01:24.869 --> 00:01:28.040
Things were looking up, but tragedy struck
from out of the blue.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.740
During a peaceful protest in the cafeteria,
a scuffle breaks out and Poussey is killed

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:38.540
when a guard restrains her, accidentally crushing
her windpipe with his knee and killing her.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.020
Abe and Glenn

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:44.479
Millions tuned in to the season 6 finale of
The Walking Dead for the moment in which the

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:48.270
gang met up with the comic book's most notorious
villain, Negan.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:52.200
It was pretty much guaranteed that at the
end of the episode, Negan would beat someone

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.780
to death with his bat, Lucille… and he did,
we just didn't get to see it.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:57.780
"You can breathe.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:00.840
You can blink.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:01.960
You can cry.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:06.979
Hell, you're all gonna be doing that."

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:11.220
It wasn't until halfway through the Season
7 premiere that we found out Negan killed

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.000
two fan-favorites — Abe and Glenn.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.110
Of course, it wasn't that simple.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.950
Abe was murdered first, and just when viewers
thought they could breathe a sigh of relief

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.820
for Glenn, who was Negan's victim in the comics,
Daryl responded to Abraham's death by punching

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.260
Negan in the face.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.380
The bad guy unleashed another dose of murderous
violence — not against Daryl, but Glenn.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.630
The brutality, and the teasing way in which
the episode doled it out, were perfectly in

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:40.220
keeping with The Walking Dead's overall arc…
but it was all still too much for more than

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.510
a few viewers to handle.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:43.510
Robert Ford

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:49.060
HBO's Westworld revolves around several main
characters who pretty much constantly die

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:54.730
and come back to life, mostly because almost
everybody is a hyper-realistic humanoid robot,

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:59.110
controlled by the the mysterious and calculating
chief robot god, Robert Ford.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:03.480
At the end of Westworld's complicated and
engrossing first season, he programmed series

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.050
star Dolores to shoot him in the head.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.050
Why?

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:11.230
In order to demonstrate that he was finally
liberating his robots, and giving them control

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:12.280
of Westworld.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:16.280
While it's always possible that it was just
a robot version of Ford that died, it isn't

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.620
likely that an actor with the stature of Sir
Anthony Hopkins would be sticking around series

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:25.450
television for long, so we're going to call
him dead … for now.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.450
Jodi Hubbard

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:32.670
CBS's sitcom Mom is a show about people struggling
with substance abuse and recovery, so it makes

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:36.860
sense that a relapse-related death would be
part of the story — even if the show is

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.210
still a laugh-track driven comedy.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:44.020
Jodi was a teenage addict in recovery, for
whom Christy served as an Alcoholics Anonymous

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.020
sponsor.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:50.330
In February 2016, Mom aired a fairly standard
wedding episode, but at the end, Christy gets

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:54.890
a phone call from police telling her that
Jodi had died from a drug overdose.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:58.830
According to co-creator Chuck Lorre, killing
off Jodi had been the plan for the character

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:03.540
since the beginning, to show that not all
recovery stories have a happy ending.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.480
Edward Meechum

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:10.420
At first just a temporary bodyguard for Frank
Underwood, Edward Meechum was a loyal, stoic,

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.070
and reliable presence.

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:17.170
He was even officially promoted to the Secret
Service when Frank Underwood became vice president,

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:18.170
and then President.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:23.410
Sadly, Edward died in the line of duty, protecting
the president when reporter-turned-cyberterrorist

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:26.610
Lucas Goodwin opened fire at a speaking engagement.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:31.110
The president took two bullets, but it was
Meechum who suffered fatal gunshot wounds.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:35.680
He died right then and there, but not before
taking out Goodwin.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:37.470
Rhonda Lyon

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:39.650
Killing off a main character in a season premiere?

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:41.430
Who do you think you are, Empire?

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.550
The Walking Dead?

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:47.960
In the Season 2 finale that aired in May 2016,
audiences were left wondering about the outcome

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:52.110
of a fight between Anika and Rhonda when somebody
falls off a balcony.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:56.380
Five months later, audiences saw Rhonda's
body embedded in a car.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:05:00.210
However, while Rhonda is definitely dead,
the character may not be.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:04.890
Showrunners have said that Andre will have
an "unusual relationship" with his dead wife,

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:10.010
so there's a good chance we'll get dream sequences,
hallucinations, and ghostly apparitions.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.330
Empire is, after all, a soap opera.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.350
Jack Pearson

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:20.810
As one of the biggest hits of the fall 2016
TV season, millions tuned in to This is Us,

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:24.720
if only to figure out what the cryptic promotional
campaign was getting at.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.990
What was the connection between a couple having
a baby in a hospital, another couple slowly

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:34.050
falling in love, a sitcom actor, and an adult
man confronting someone who appeared to be

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.050
his father?

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:39.170
Because the show unfolds over the course of
three decades, character deaths are a given,

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:43.740
but one of them is pretty startling: it's
revealed that Milo Ventimiglia's Jack isn't

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:48.790
part of any modern storylines, because he
died and was cremated at some point in the

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:49.790
past.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.420
Because of the way the show is presented,
we'll still see plenty of Jack.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:56.870
Still, it's pretty sad for audiences knowing
what he doesn't know — that he won't live

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.070
to see his kids grow up.

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:00.550
Margaery and Tommen

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:05.650
After falling under the control of the High
Sparrow, everything went up in green flames

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:10.320
for Margaery, her life becoming collateral
damage at the hands of her vengeful mother-in-law.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:15.820
Cersei Lannister blew up the whole of King's
Landing with some heretofore undiscovered

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:16.820
Wildfire.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:21.240
And Cersei's son, King Tommen, was pretty
upset after the death of his bride, so he

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.700
went for a walk.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.970
Out a window.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.020
Ah, well.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:30.320
Thanks for watching!

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.350
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:36.060
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

